cruiser: lift the D-Bus display listener's refresh cap to ~100fps.

Upstream dbus listeners are pinned to GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT (30ms ≈
33fps) — fine for a GUI menu bar, but it caps the dmabuf viewer (viewer-dd)
at ~33fps. 10ms lifts the cap to ~100fps. Applied by build.mts after
extract; without it the dmabuf viewer still works, just slower.

--- a/ui/dbus-listener.c
+++ b/ui/dbus-listener.c
@@ -1281,6 +1281,10 @@
     }
 #endif
     qemu_console_register_listener(con, &ddl->dcl, ops);
+    /* cruiser: local dmabuf listeners want tighter pacing than the
+     * 30ms default (33fps) — the dbus display is a dedicated local
+     * viewer, so cap at 100fps rather than the shared-GUI default. */
+    qemu_console_listener_set_refresh(&ddl->dcl, 10);
 
     return ddl;
 }
